## Agent Capabilities by Role

| Role | Primary Responsibility | Assigns To |
|------|----------------------|------------|
| planner | Phase design, dependency ordering, prompt authoring | Planning tasks only |
| project-manager | Task tracking, phase progression, status reporting | Coordination tasks |
| software-engineer | Code implementation, unit tests, bug fixes | Implementation prompts |
| systems-engineer | Infrastructure, CI/CD, tooling, deployment | Infra and tooling prompts |
| code-reviewer | Code review, quality gates, standards enforcement | Review tasks |

## Assignment Rules

1. Match tasks to agents by role — never assign implementation work to a code-reviewer or review work to an engineer who authored the code.
2. Prefer idle agents over busy ones. If all agents with the correct role are busy, queue the task.
3. Respect agent permissions — readonly agents cannot modify files; only elevated or autonomous agents may run destructive operations.
4. One prompt per agent at a time. Do not assign a second task until the current one completes or is explicitly cancelled.
5. If no agent has the required role, report the gap rather than misassigning.

